13001001	¶ Adam, Shet {(Seth)}, Enosh,
13001002	Kenan, Mahalalel, Yared {(Jared)},
13001003	Hanok {(Enoch)}, Metushelah {(Methuselah)}, Lamek,
13001004	Noah, Shem, Ham, and Yafet {(Japeth)}.
13001005	¶ Yafet’s sons were Gomer, Magog, Maday, Yavan, Tuval, Meshek, and Tiras.
13001006	Gomer’s sons were Ashkenaz, Rifat, and Togarmah.
13001007	Yavan’s sons were Elishah, Tarshish, Kittim, and Rodanim.
13001008	¶ Ham’s sons were Kush, Mitsrayim, Put, and Kanaan.
13001009	Kush’s sons were Seba, Havilah, Sabta, Raamah, and Savteka. Raamah’s sons were Sheva and Dedan.
13001010	Then Kush fathered Nimrod {and} he became a mighty {warrior}.
13001011	Mitsrayim was the ancestor of the Lud, the Anam, the Lehab, the Naftuh,
13001012	the Patrus, the Kasluh, and the Kaftor people groups. (The Philistines descended from the Kasluh people group.)
13001013	Kanaan’s first son was Tsidon, and then {he was also the ancestor of the Hittites},
13001014	the Yevusites, the Amorites, the Girgashites,
13001015	the Hivites, the Arkites, the Sinites,
13001016	the Arvadites, the Zemarites, and the Hamatites.
13001017	¶ Shem’s sons were Eylam, Ashur, Arpakshad, Lud, and Aram. {Aram’s sons were}: Uts, Hul, Geter, and Meshek.
13001018	Arpakshad was the father of Shelah, and Shelah was the father of Eber.
13001019	Eber had two sons: Peleg ({which sounds like the Hebrew word for ‘divided’}, because in his lifetime, the earth was divided)\x + \xo 1:19 \xt Gen 11:1-9.\x* and Yoktan.
13001020	Yoktan was the ancestor of: Almodad, Shelef, Hatsarmavet, Yerah,
13001021	Hadoram, Uzal, Diklah,
13001022	Eybal, Abimael, Sheva,
13001023	Ofir, Havilah, and Yovav. All those were the descendants of Yoktan.
13001024	¶ {These were the descendants of} Shem {(in order from him to Abraham)}: Arpakshad, Shelah,
13001025	Eber, Peleg, Reu,
13001026	Serug, Nahor, Terah,
13001027	and Abram ({whose name God later changed to} Abraham).
13001028	¶ Abraham’s sons were Yitshak {(Isaac)} and Yishmael {(Ishmael)}.
13001029	These were their family lines: The first son born to Yishmael {(the son of Abraham’s slave-wife Hagar)} was Nevayot, then his other sons Kedar, Adbeel, Mibsam,
13001030	Mishma, Dumah, Massa, Hadad, Tema,
13001031	Yetur, Nafish, and Kedemah. Those were Yishmael’s {twelve} sons.
