13001042	Etser’s sons were Bilhan, Zaavan, and Yaakan. Dishan’s sons were Uts and Aran.
13001043	¶ These are the kings who ruled the region of Edom {(where Seir’s descendants lived)} before any kings ruled over Yisrael: Bela son of Beor, and his city’s name was Dinhavah.
13001044	When Bela died, Zerah’s son Yovav from Batsrah {city} {replaced him as king}.
13001045	When Yovav died, Husham {replaced him as king}. He was from the region where the Teman people group lived.
13001046	When Husham died, Bedad’s son Hadad {replaced him as king}. His city’s name was Avit. Hadad defeated the Midyan people group in the Moav region.
13001047	When Hadad died, Samlah from Masrekah {city} {replaced him as king}.
13001048	When Samlah died, Shaul from Rehovot-on-the-river {replaced him as king}.
13001049	When Shaul died, Akbor’s son Baal-Hanan {replaced him as king}.
13001050	When Baal-Hanan died, Hadad {replaced him as king}. His city’s name was Pa’u. His wife’s name was Meheytavel—she was the daughter of Matred {and the granddaughter} of Me-Zahab.
