13002017	Avigayil had Amasa. Amasa’s father was Yeter, a descendant of Yishmael {(Ishmael)}.
13002018	¶ Hetsron’s {third} son Kalev {(Caleb)} had sons with Azuvah, one of his wives. The sons were Yesher, Shovav, and Ardon. (The other wife’s name was Yeriot.)
13002019	When Azuvah died, Kalev married Efrat, and they had a son named Hur.
13002020	Hur was the father of Uri, and Uri was the father of Betsal’el.
13002021	¶ Later, when Hetsron was sixty years old, he {had sexual intercourse} with a daughter of Makir from the region of Gilead and married her. {Hetsron’s new wife} gave birth to {their son} Seguv.
13002022	Seguv was the father of Yair, and Yair controlled twenty-three cities in the Gilead region.
13002023	{But} Geshur and Aram captured Havvot-Yair and Kenat from them, plus {their surrounding towns}—sixty towns {in all,} {populated by} descendants of Makir (the father of Gilead).
