21001001	¶ {The following} are the words of the leader,\f + \fr 1:1 \ft We don’t have enough information to fully understand the meaning of the Hebrew word ‘קֹהֶ֣לֶת’ (Kohelet), but it probably means something like ‘leader/speaker of the assembly’, so we use ‘the leader’ throughout this document.\f* David’s son, king in Yerushalem {(Jerusalem)}:
21001002	₁ “Totally pointless,” says the leader.₁ “{A complete waste of time}. Everything’s worthless.”
21001003	₁ What profit does humanity gain from all {their hard work in this world}?
21001004	₁ {Generations come, and generations go},₁ {but the world just carries on going}.
21001005	₁ The sun rises and the sun sets,₁ then {rushes} {around} to its place, rising there {again}.
21001006	₁ Going to the south then around to the north,₁ the wind is going, changing, turning,₁ then {it’s} returning on its rounds.
21001007	₁ All the rivers {flow into} the sea {but it never gets} full.₁ The place that the rivers are going to, they {end up} going {there} again.
21001008	₁ Everything is wearisome—{not even worth talking about}.₁ The {eyes} {never stop} seeing,₁ and {your} {ears} {never fill up with everything they hear}.
21001009	₁ Whatever that was {in the past}, it will be {in the future},₁ and {everything that’s happened before, will happen} {again}.₁ There’s nothing new {in this world}.\f + \fr 1:9 \ft ‘Under the sun’ isn’t a natural English idiom\f*
21001010	₁ If someone says, “Look at this—it’s new,”₁ {well}, it was already done {long ago before we even got here}.
21001011	₁ {Things that happened in the past get forgotten},₁ and {the same will also happen for future events}.₁ {People in the future will be exactly the same}.
21001012	₁ I, the leader, was king over Yisrael in Yerushalem.
21001013	₁ I {used my mind and} wisdom to discover and to explore everything that is done {in this world}.₁ It’s a difficult job that God has given humanity to be busy with.
21001014	₁ I saw everything that gets done {in this world},₁ and look—everything’s pointless {like} chasing after the wind.
21001015	₁ Something that’s bent can’t be straightened {again},₁ and what’s missing can’t be counted.
21001016	₁ I spoke with {sincerity}, saying, “Look at me—I’ve become {powerful},₁ and I’ve {increased in wisdom relative to everyone who ruled before me} {here} in Yerushalem.\x + \xo 1:16: \xt 1Ki 4:29-31.\x*₁ {My mind has acquired} much knowledge and wisdom.”
21001017	₁ I {made it my aim to discover} knowledge and wisdom {versus} madness and folly.₁ I was aware that that also is chasing after the wind
21001018	₁ because {having much wisdom leads to much frustration}₁ and anyone who’s adding knowledge is {also} adding pain.
21002001	¶ I said {to myself},₁ “Come on, let me {find out what’s good and enjoy the pleasure from them}.”₁ But look, it was also pointless.
21002002	₁ To laughter, I said, “It’s madness,”₁ and to joy, “What’s {the point of this}?”
21002003	₁ I explored in myself how to {indulge my body} with wine, but my {mind} was guiding me in wisdom.₁ {Also,} how to grasp foolishness₁ until I could see whether that’s better for humanity to do {while they live out their lives here on this earth}.
21002004	₁ I expanded my {program of works}.₁ I built houses for myself.₁ I planted vineyards for myself.\x + \xo 2:4-8: \xt 1Ki 10:23-27; 2Ch 9:22-27.\x*
21002005	₁ I made gardens for myself, and royal parks,₁ and I planted {all different kinds} of fruit trees in them.
21002006	₁ I constructed pools for myself₁ to {irrigate} a forest of growing trees.
21002007	₁ I acquired male and female servants,₁ and {the children born to them} belonged to me.₁ Also {a large number} of sheep and cattle belonged to me—₁ more than all {my predecessors} in Yerushalem.\x + \xo 2:7: \xt 1Ki 4:23.\x*
21002008	₁ I also accumulated gold and silver for myself,₁ and treasure from kings and from the provinces.₁ I appointed male and female singers for myself,₁ and the pleasures of the sons of humanity—{many women}.\x + \xo 2:8: \xt 1Ki 10:10,14-22.\x*
21002009	₁ {So I became famous},₁ and I added more than all who {preceded me} in Yerushalem.₁ Also my wisdom stayed with me.\x + \xo 2:9: \xt 1Ch 29:25.\x*
21002010	₁ {Everything my eyes wanted}, I {gave} them.₁ I didn’t {hold back} from {anything that would make me happy},₁ because {I was happy inside} from all my work₁ and that was my reward from all my effort.
21002011	₁ And I turned, I, to all {the things that I’d made}₁ and to the work that I’d done,₁ and look, everything was pointless and chasing after the wind,₁ and there wasn’t any profit {in anything done in this world}.
21002012	¶ Then I {changed direction to investigate} wisdom and madness and folly,₁ because what could {any future} king do that hasn’t already been done?
21002013	₁ I saw that wisdom {is to be preferred over} folly,₁ just as light {is to be preferred} over darkness.
21002014	₁ {The wise person uses their} eyes,₁ {but} the fool walks in the darkness,₁ and even I know that {the same fate comes} to both of them.
