21003001	¶ There’s an appointed time for everything,₁ and an appropriate time for every activity {in this world}:
21003002	₁ A time to give birth and a time to die.₁ A time to plant and a time to pull out what was planted.
21003003	₁ A time to kill and a time to heal.₁ A time to tear down and a time to build up.
21003004	₁ A time to cry and a time to laugh.₁ A time to mourn and a time to dance.
21003005	₁ A time to throw stones and a time to pick up stones.₁ A time to embrace and a time to avoid embracing.
21003006	₁ A time to search and a time to lose.₁ A time to keep and a time to toss out.
21003007	₁ A time to tear and a time to mend.₁ A time to be silent and a time to speak up.
21003008	₁ A time to love and a time to hate.₁ A time for war and a time for peace.
21003009	¶ What {do people gain from all the work they do}?
21003010	₂ I’ve seen the task that God has given people to {keep them occupied}.
21003011	₁ {God} makes everything {happen at the appropriate} time.₁ Also, he puts {the awareness of} eternity into {the human mind},₁ yet humanity can’t grasp {what} God has done from {the} beginning to {the} end.
21003012	₁ I know that there’s nothing better for them₁ than being cheerful and doing good during {their lives}
21003013	₁ and everyone should eat and drink and see good in {everything they do}—₁ that’s a gift from God.
21003014	₁ I know that everything God does will be enduring.₁ There’s nothing that needs to be added to it, or taken away,₁ and God has {done it like that so that people will respect and want to obey him}.
21003015	₁ Whatever there is, it already was,₁ and whatever is to be, it already is,₁ and God will {watch whatever’s being worked on}.
21003016	₁ Then again I saw {in this world} at the place of judgement, there was wickedness,₁ and at the place of righteousness, there was wickedness.
21003017	₁ I said {to myself}, “God will judge the righteous and the wicked,₁ because there’s a time for every matter, and {for every action to be judged}.”
21003018	₁ I said {to myself}, “God tests humanity₁ so they can see that they themselves are {like} animals
21003019	₁ because the {same one thing happens to both people and animals}:₁ {just like one dies, so does the other}—they both have the same breath.₁ {But people have no} advantage over {animals}—everything is pointless.
21003020	₁ Both go to {the same} place—₁ both {came} from the dust and both return to the dust.
